xnu 0368: inject the probe into the Photos app

Measured 2026-11-18: MobileSlideShow execs and dies `sig 6` with the same pc, lr
and backtrace on every launch, before its scene appears, and the ring carries no
line from inside it because `mondrian_probe_target()` names the daemons and not
the app. The exception is the thing to read, and it is read the same way assetsd's
death was named: `MONDRIAN THROW` prints the name and the reason where the stack
still exists.

It also matters that the app carries the hook at all. The TCC stand-in in the
hook answers `TCCAccessRequest`, which is the call whose denial aborts a client;
a process without the dylib keeps the real answer, which on this port is a denial
(tccd refuses it even though SecTask reads the entitlement through the audit
token). assetsd already survives its own check with the stand-in in place, so the
app is the next process that needs the same treatment.

--- a/bsd/kern/kern_exec.c
+++ b/bsd/kern/kern_exec.c
@@ -5690,6 +5690,14 @@
 		"PhotosFileProvider",
 		"photolibraryd",
 		"iconservicesagent",
+		/*
+		 * The app itself, measured 2026-11-18: it execs and dies `sig 6`
+		 * with the same pc, lr and backtrace on every launch, before its
+		 * scene appears, and the ring carries no line from inside it
+		 * because nothing in it was ours. assetsd's death was named by the
+		 * throw hook; this one needs the same.
+		 */
+		"MobileSlideShow",
 	};
 	size_t i;
 
